{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "01RI", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-dominant}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:136a9425d2faed5e0d5ada4df18ac1925a9a8ef9eabb754370cef763b28b8c79", "source_text": "Dominant morphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:771955b56245744cea683e775a45e87eb6ff5f4371e7dae96906453390299507", "unit_id": "tag:01RI:title"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01RI", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8a4b765b91cf0347ca31501c857a112b069c6a920061a2dc7c5e1213a54baefd", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe definition of a morphism of schemes being dominant is a little\ndifferent from what you might expect if you are used to the notion\nof a dominant morphism of varieties.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b0cce34818f9169efea1174b159713ee3140ef5576aa64540c22930689cade87", "unit_id": "tag:01RI:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01RI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-dominant}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cb241c2264af61eb509116a202113df3facf0710d61998243e8d3c084777c72b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:feec50fe0bb62e474c8e3b22ce7e2c369fd8e76b6ff207a4e6ac1dc7ef9abd79", "source_text": "A morphism <MATH_0001> of schemes is called <TEXTITOPEN_0001>dominant<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if the\nimage of <MATH_0002> is a dense subset of <MATH_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fc47116a3d62aec06e8bd756d59bbe8c0ef34653db339c1a1a49890c5acf52ae", "unit_id": "tag:01RJ:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01RI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$k$", "MATH_0002": "$\\lambda_1, \\lambda_2, \\ldots$", "MATH_0003": "$k$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\coprod\\nolimits_{i = 1, 2, \\ldots } \\Spec(k)\n\\longrightarrow\n\\Spec(k[x])\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$i$", "MATH_0006": "$x = \\lambda_i$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9d2c9a0f73d7932b3a0d99dd3dbd8be256b389b55252ac905da1e4f62794f332", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c85ef53a4701815cbcdae398495ddf5584659d4d3afb07b2d1187d00152d0994", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nSo for example, if <MATH_0001> is an infinite field and <MATH_0002>\nis a countable collection of distinct elements of <MATH_0003>, then the morphism\n<MATH_0004>\nwith <MATH_0005>th factor mapping to the point <MATH_0006> is dominant.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:178f2395337ac3af11bb7e6e17b6b85aa3676e9817dadc9dfda59f2b543e0727", "unit_id": "tag:01RI:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01RI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-generic-points-in-image-dominant}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fd565504f9e95205624be6bb38f157401ad514610ecd77d0ee29bbd7623a40cc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8953404bb14afcf28f95fb7da57e6df8ff42d94773b4600a160e4e8effca65d4", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nIf every generic point of every irreducible component of <MATH_0002>\nis in the image of <MATH_0003>, then <MATH_0004> is dominant.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:decfc3dd8c31b101728f4c78d28fd2954d332a96249cbf18be4de84ccb4604bf", "unit_id": "tag:01RK:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01RI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-scheme-sober}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{topology-lemma-irreducible}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3373d69d1a771d1b240d3f94798edce7e161caf54de4b2de49dd8524c8dc1502", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:42dacfef70db6cf70dfd05a92c7543b7b0d742b9120f2f8d6a8f335a9c6170c1", "source_text": "This is a topological fact which follows directly from the fact that\nthe topological space underlying a scheme is sober, see\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0001>, and that\nevery point of <MATH_0001> is contained in an irreducible component of\n<MATH_0002>, see Topology, Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d4ce1c82d62ee971c493a856b6e2770b730ba26f375ea9209528a694a9e0c85c", "unit_id": "tag:01RK:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01RI", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8a4b765b91cf0347ca31501c857a112b069c6a920061a2dc7c5e1213a54baefd", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe expectation that morphisms are dominant only if generic points of the\ntarget are in the image does hold if the morphism is quasi-compact.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2b414fbbab50230f8e7557f8a630a189efbfaaebeaaee49fe122153abfcaa64b", "unit_id": "tag:01RI:prose-0003"}
